      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): preserve primitive tool result output",
        "body": "Closes #99523\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running tools that return primitive string results could lose useful tool output when the agent prepared visible/model-readable result text. It also prevents successful structured output from being promoted into an error message when the result is not marked as an error.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe tool result text extractor now preserves safe primitive string output before object-only result handling. Error message extraction now only falls back to normalized result text for results that are explicitly classified as tool errors, keeping successful structured output out of the error channel.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now see and continue from tools that return plain string output, while successful tool results no longer appear as synthetic error text.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused regression test on this PR branch:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/test-projects.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.tools.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       37 passed (37)\n```\n\nRedacted runtime proof from a private gateway deployment after applying the same helper-path fix. Hostnames, IP addresses, local filesystem paths, and private deployment identifiers are intentionally omitted:\n\n```text\nprimitiveString.visibleOutput=plain result\ndetailsStructured.visibleOutput={\"details\":{\"status\":\"ok\",\"result\":{\"messageId\":\"msg-1\",\"delivered\":true}}}\nrootStructured.visibleOutput={\"ok\":true,\"value\":42}\nimageOnly.visibleOutput=undefined\nsuccessfulStructured.errorMessage=undefined\n```\n\nThis verifies the changed behavior beyond the unit test boundary: primitive string tool results produce visible output, safe structured output remains visible, image-only content is not converted into text, and successful structured output is not reported as an error.\n",
        "branch": "fix/tool-result-output-clean",
